# Lofree HYZEN67 (388d:0025 via its 2.4 GHz dongle, 388d:0024 over USB cable):
# drop the key its Consumer Control interface sends on its own, with no physical press, exactly ~20 min after the last real
# keypress -- the keyboard entering its "Level 2 sleep" (set to 20 min in the
# Lofree web configurator). Linux has no name for it (KEY_UNKNOWN, 240), but
# it still counts as input, so it woke the displays and kept the OLED TV on.
#
# Captured 2026-11-02 with scancode c0cff (HID Consumer page, usage 0x0cff) at
# 20:12:04 and 20:56:44, each 20m04s after the last keypress. "reserved" maps it
# to KEY_RESERVED, which libinput and the compositor ignore. Physical keys that
# also come through as KEY_UNKNOWN (c04b0, c0401) are left alone.
#
# The cable ID is covered too (added 2026-11-03) since the keyboard is sometimes
# plugged in to charge; the phantom key was only ever captured on the dongle.
#
# After editing: sudo systemd-hwdb update && sudo udevadm trigger -s input
evdev:input:b0003v388Dp0024*
evdev:input:b0003v388Dp0025*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_c0cff=reserved
